+-- r5 (Opus B1, Fable B1, Codex S1; Kyle, K-10): one split of what is taken
+-- back under a payment's posting entry between the payment and its
+-- overpayment credit, read by both positions and both caps. Each row of the
+-- entry's tree, in recorded order, gets the part the credit absorbs:
+--   * a row recorded before the credit: none (the credit was sized after it);
+--   * a row taking money back: first what the credit still held at the row's
+--     instant, then what the payment's own part still held; what neither
+--     held (K-10: what was paid out stands) falls on the credit as far as its
+--     amount, then on the payment;
+--   * a row giving money back: to the credit first, as far as it absorbed.
+-- Held means the amount less what was absorbed and what was given at that
+-- instant (cash_drawn_at). Rows of one instant (one transaction) read as if
+-- the row under the entry came last; the caps also hold the payment and its
+-- credit together (check_cash_source), so any reading of one instant keeps
+-- K-10's refund cap.
+CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.overpayment_split(p_credit_id uuid)
+    RETURNS TABLE (id uuid, on_date date, amount numeric, absorbed numeric, created_at timestamp with time zone)
+    LANGUAGE plpgsql STABLE
